mb</span>)</span> <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">inv</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a> <span class=\"fn\">b'</span>)</span></span>\n      | <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Core.html#ForInStep.done\">ForInStep.done</a> <span class=\"fn\">b'</span></span> =&gt; <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">inv</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a> <span class=\"fn\">b'</span></span></span></span><a href=\"./Std/WP/Triple/Basic.html#Std.WP.Triple\">;</a>       <span class=\"fn\">einv</span> <a href=\"./Std/WP/Triple/Basic.html#Std.WP.Triple\">⦄</a></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Std/WP/Triple/Basic.html#Std.WP.Triple\">⦃</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">inv</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a> <span class=\"fn\">init</span></span> <a href=\"./Std/WP/Triple/Basic.html#Std.WP.Triple\">⦄</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Core.html#ForIn.forIn\">forIn</a> <span class=\"fn\">l</span> <span class=\"fn\">init</span> <span class=\"fn\">f</span></span> <a href=\"./Std/WP/Triple/Basic.html#Std.WP.Triple\">⦃</a> <span class=\"fn\">fun (<span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <span class=\"fn\">β</span>) =&gt; <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">inv</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span></span><a href=\"./Std/WP/Triple/Basic.html#Std.WP.Triple\">;</a> <span class=\"fn\">einv</span> <a href=\"./Std/WP/Triple/Basic.html#Std.WP.Triple\">⦄</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Specification for `forIn` over a `Lean.Loop`. The invariant takes the loop's `exit` flag:\n`inv false b` means \"still iterating with `b`\", `inv true b` means \"finished with result `b`\".\n","docLink":"./Std/WP/Triple/SpecLemmas.html#Std.WP.Spec.forIn_loop","kind":"theorem","line":2204,"name":"Std.WP.Spec.forIn_loop","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/470d5ce1400764999581fd26d5d72b00d990b0f4/src/Std/WP/Triple/SpecLemmas.lean#L2204-L2239"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">noncomputable abbrev</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/Triple/SpecLemmas.html#Std.WP.WhileInvariant.ofInvariantAndBreak\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">WP</span>.<span class=\"name\">WhileInvariant</span>.<span class=\"name\">ofInvariantAndBreak</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α </span><span class=\"fn\">Pred</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/WP/Assertion.html#Std.WP.Assertion\">Assertion</a> <span class=\"fn\">Pred</span></span>]</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">inv </span><span class=\"fn\">onBreak</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">α</span> → <span class=\"fn\">Pred</span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/WP/Triple/SpecLemmas.html#Std.WP.WhileInvariant\">WhileInvariant</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">Pred</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Construct an invariant from a loop invariant `inv` and a break condition `onBreak`.\n\n`inv` holds at the end of every loop iteration (including the breaking one), and `onBreak` holds in\naddition to `inv` once the loop is done. For a normal `while` loop `onBreak` can be taken as the\nnegation of the loop condition.\n","docLink":"./Std/WP/Triple/SpecLemmas.html#Std.WP.WhileInvariant.ofInvariantAndBreak","kind":"def","line":2190,"name":"Std.WP.WhileInvariant.ofInvariantAndBreak","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/470d5ce1400764999581fd26d5d72b00d990b0f4/src/Std/WP/Triple/SpecLemmas.lean#L2190-L2201"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><s